%description:

What a second cell costs the first, against the closed form.

Interference is the least covered part of the radio model -- no shipped
fingerprint row varies downlinkInterference at all -- and it is the code a
structural change to the medium disturbs most, because it is the one place
where a cell reaches into another cell's channel model.

The scenario is two cells and one victim UE, run with downlinkInterference
off and on. Every random ingredient is switched off, so both the wanted
signal and the interferer's contribution are the same closed-form budget the
LinkBudget test grades, evaluated at their two distances:

    S = txPower - PL(d_serving)     + Gtx + Grx - cableLoss
    I = txPower - PL(d_interferer)  + Gtx + Grx - cableLoss
    N = thermalNoise + noiseFigure

    SINR = S - 10 log10( 10^(N/10) + 10^(I/10) )

The interfering cell is loaded, but a scheduler does not fill every band in
every TTI, and the model only counts a band that the interferer actually
occupied (computeDownlinkInterference checks getDlBandStatus). The reported
SINR is therefore not one number -- which is what makes the extremes the
right thing to assert, and makes them exact:

 - the maximum is the interference-free budget, from the TTIs in which the
   interferer happened to be idle;
 - the minimum is the fully-loaded budget, from the TTIs in which it used
   every band.

Both are predicted, so the check does not depend on how the load happened to
fall, only on the two endpoints being reached. With interference off the two
extremes collapse onto one value, which is also what proves the machinery is
genuinely off rather than merely quiet.

%extraargs: -c InterferenceDelta

%file: demo.xml
<config>
    <interface among='eNB* eNodeB* enb* *Enb* gNB* gNodeB* gnb* *Gnb* upf* *Upf* mecHost* pgw*' address='10.x.x.x' netmask='255.255.255.0'/>
    <interface hosts='*' address='192.168.x.x' netmask='255.255.255.0'/>
</config>

%inifile: omnetpp.ini

[Config InterferenceDelta]
network = simu5g.simulations.nr.networks.MultiCell_Standalone
sim-time-limit = 3s
**.routingRecorder.enabled = false
cmdenv-express-mode = true
cmdenv-status-frequency = 10000000s

output-scalar-file = results/${iterationvarsf}${repetition}.sca
output-vector-file = results/${iterationvarsf}${repetition}.vec
**.vector-recording = false
# The extremes are the quantities under test here, not the average.
**.measuredSinrDl.result-recording-modes = mean,count,min,max

############### The sweep: the one thing that varies ##############
**.downlinkInterference = ${dli = false, true}
**.uplinkInterference = false
**.bgCellInterference = false
**.extCellInterference = false

############### Geometry: victim 100 m from its cell, 400 m from the other ##############
*.gnb1.mobility.initialX = 250m
*.gnb1.mobility.initialY = 500m
*.gnb1.mobility.initialZ = 10m
*.gnb2.mobility.initialX = 750m
*.gnb2.mobility.initialY = 500m
*.gnb2.mobility.initialZ = 10m
*.numUe = 2
*.ue[*].servingNodeId = 0
*.ue[*].nrServingNodeId = 1
# Association is by best signal and then frozen: the victim must not change
# cell halfway through, or the budget it is graded against changes with it.
**.dynamicCellAssociation = true
**.enableHandover = false
*.ue[0].mobility.initialX = 350m
*.ue[0].mobility.initialY = 500m
*.ue[0].mobility.initialZ = 1.5m
*.ue[1].mobility.initialX = 750m
*.ue[1].mobility.initialY = 500m
*.ue[1].mobility.initialZ = 1.5m
**.mobility.constraintAreaMinX = 0m
**.mobility.constraintAreaMinY = 0m
**.mobility.constraintAreaMinZ = 0m
**.mobility.constraintAreaMaxX = 1500m
**.mobility.constraintAreaMaxY = 1000m
**.mobility.constraintAreaMaxZ = 50m
**.mobility.initFromDisplayString = false

############### The channel: one path loss and nothing else ##############
**.scenario = "URBAN_MICROCELL"
**.nodebHeight = 10m
**.ueHeight = 1.5m
**.dynamicLos = false
**.fixedLos = true
**.fading = false
**.shadowing = false

############### The budget terms, stated rather than inherited ##############
*.carrierAggregation.numComponentCarriers = 1
*.carrierAggregation.componentCarrier[0].carrierFrequency = 2GHz
*.carrierAggregation.componentCarrier[0].numBands = 6
**.numBands = 6
**.eNodeBTxPower = 40dBm
**.antennGainEnB = 18dBi
**.antennaGainUe = 0dBi
**.cableLoss = 2dB
**.thermalNoise = -104.5dBm
**.ueNoiseFigure = 7dBm

############### Traffic: a trickle to the victim, a flood to the other cell ##############
*.ue[*].numApps = 1
*.server.numApps = 2
*.ue[*].app[0].typename = "CbrReceiver"
*.ue[*].app[0].localPort = 3000
*.server.app[*].typename = "CbrSender"
*.server.app[0].destAddress = "ue[0]"
*.server.app[0].destPort = 3000
*.server.app[0].localPort = 3088
*.server.app[0].packetSize = 40B
*.server.app[0].samplingTime = 0.02s
*.server.app[0].startTime = 0.1s
# Enough to keep gnb2 busy most of the time, but not so much that it never
# falls idle: the check needs both extremes to occur.
*.server.app[1].destAddress = "ue[1]"
*.server.app[1].destPort = 3000
*.server.app[1].localPort = 3089
*.server.app[1].packetSize = 1000B
*.server.app[1].samplingTime = 0.0002s
*.server.app[1].startTime = 0.05s

*.configurator.config = xmldoc("./demo.xml")

%postrun-command: ../../physics_reference.py --grade results >verdict.txt

%contains: verdict.txt
graded=6 failures=0

%not-contains: verdict.txt
FAILED
